id: pm-rl-measured-influence
title: Measure evaluation sensitivity to declared training slices
description: "Run explicitly budgeted omission and integer reweighting experiments for declared training slices; retain exact checkpoints and measured per-evaluation associations, and carry bounded evidence into the next proposal."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: evaluation,influence,training
created_at: "2026-10-29T08:20:10.275Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T13:09:27.016Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Reports reproduce on a fixed learner and seed; Held-out data never enters training; Exhausted experiment budgets return partial evidence without a ranking claim; Typed SDK and compact CLI output, audit records, recursive proposal evidence, non-git public-copy validation, seeded model tests and npm plus Bun release gates"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T08:20:18.810Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current core CLI/SDK, pm-rl policy-card.ts and evaluation-plan.ts, and pm-jev counterfactual.ts. Core owns native records/history/locks; policy cards explain provenance and validity; Jev removes inference evidence. This feature measures retraining sensitivity. Preserve all normal proposal, evaluation, promotion and feedback gates. Results remain associations; no causal identification claim. Current published CLI is 2026.10.28; package SDK remains pinned 2026.10.25."
  "2026-10-29T08:28:28.000Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the first typed request/report schema and fixed seeded retraining using the existing bandit kernel. Integer multiplicities implement omissions/reweighting; exact integer budgets include the baseline. Numerical tests confirm deterministic checkpoints, changed held-out scores without changed fitted parameters, strict dense/finite admission, and partial evidence with ranking=null. Native report identity is immutable; proposal evidence cites a certified SDK history revision and is retained in seed/candidate provenance. No shared experiment budget, plan replay or new promotion authority is introduced."
  "2026-10-29T08:46:27.483Z",codex-agent,"Public-copy validation passed on unbraind/pm-ops at ba05bb8b96b313b86d25896ef40880712f295881: 162 items, 116 training, 46 held out, 42 held-out done-role items (SDK registry semantics). Four fits used 2048 samples and 32 updates; overall expected-reward deltas were +0.004185111930395058, -0.003866597213557754 and -0.0010403833570880039. The two-fit budget retained two named omissions without a ranking. Source fingerprint stayed unchanged across 332 read-only files. Both recursive generations promoted through existing gates and both replayed on resume with the same final checkpoint. Git was absent from PATH. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy removed training-slice membership effects: the deterministic movement test failed 0/1, then restored behavior passed 1/1. See docs/training-influence-evidence.json and docs/training-influence-revert.json."
  "2026-10-29T09:02:33.251Z",codex-agent,"The captured tarball passed all five supported host acquisition modes on CLI 2026.10.28: npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx and project-local. Every mode ran with Git absent, returned two measured comparisons, preserved idempotent retry, carried proposal evidence, and reported two omissions at a one-fit budget. Compact show output measured 1133 JSON bytes and 837 TOON bytes. Artifact contents and SHA-256 are recorded in docs/training-influence-packed.json. Stateful model validation uses pm test with pm_context_mode=none and workspace_context_mode=snapshot; after an expensive run was interrupted, redundant history/proposal replays were reduced while retaining all 500 SDK read-back sequences and all native fields/relationships in the model. Native SDK item creation arbitrates collisions; no lock-based isolation from workspace transactions is claimed, and the remaining post-read ordinary-writer window is documented."
  "2026-10-29T09:18:27.831Z",codex-agent,"Targeted native validation passed 7/7 via pm test --run --progress in a non-git snapshot workspace: all 500 seeded operation sequences completed and read state back through the SDK, including old-input replays, CRLF/whitespace, native annotations, relationships, custom status ids and ambient focus. Real SDK peers were injected at every measured read/write boundary for report creation and proposal feedback. An additional latest boundary run passed 3/3, including signed-zero normalization through the producer JSON wire format and malformed emitted-number refusals. Typecheck, test compilation and lint passed; duplicate and docstring gates passed without threshold changes. Final npm and Bun full-gate evidence will come from CI on the PR head, with URLs/counts recorded in the PR to keep tracker writes complete before final-head verification."
  "2026-10-29T09:40:37.358Z",codex-agent,"Final captured artifact passed all five npm/Bun global, ephemeral and local installation modes with Git absent. SHA-256 e68d259465fadd8ada8aab58374d7c177d59c83db03a7f3bf2ff36cf5a22d695, 816499 bytes; contents include the typed SDK module, CLI, example and documentation. SDK source-copy validation was independently compared byte-for-byte with all 332 tracker files at the declared public commit. Isolated strict tracker health passes; the existing development extension skew and legacy advisories are recorded on pm-rl-9uz4. Releasing this agent claim for ready-PR handoff; leave the feature open for orchestrator verification. Final-head full npm and Bun CI run URL/counts will be recorded in the PR, with no later tracker writes."
  "2026-10-29T09:53:43.047Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK contract inspection found that compact history index is a physical row position, while version is the durable address after native compaction (HistoryDiffEntry.version and HistoryResult.version_addressing). Correcting report citations to prefer version with an un-compacted index fallback; adding a real SDK compaction fixture and a durable-version oracle. Only new disposable fixture history is compacted; repository histories remain byte-prefix extensions. This is a package compatibility correction, not an SDK gap."
  "2026-10-29T10:07:39.067Z",codex-agent,"Durable-version compatibility regression passed 1/1 on a new non-git SDK fixture after native compaction. The independent oracle is HistoryResult.version_addressing.last_version. Reverting only readTrainingInfluence to physical row indices fails 0/1; restored behavior passes 1/1. The original training-slice behavioral revert also still fails 0/1 and restores 1/1. Updated artifact 77167abc786e877a710036fe2a98827991333fd850a0f7e553016c702826bc8d (816521 bytes) passed all five complete packed acquisition modes. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, duplicate and docstring checks pass. This correction supersedes the earlier frozen head and requires fresh final-head CI; final URL/counts remain in PR 119. No tracked history was compacted or rewritten."
  "2026-10-29T10:39:04.942Z",codex-agent,"Required final-head CI monitoring cutoff reached after 30 minutes for implementation head 5d7477a7a18b320dcf2d4466ccb6b872f57186b2. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/40855159641 still has test (22), test (26) and Bun release (26) queued: 0/3 release jobs completed, no final-head test or coverage totals available. This is pending evidence, not approval. Earlier run 40851706089 was superseded and canceled after the durable-version correction. This tracking-only receipt changes no implementation or packaged bytes; its push may queue a further check run. Leave the item open and the agent claim released. The orchestrator must wait for exact-head npm/Bun gates before closing or merging."
  "2026-10-29T11:06:50.785Z",codex-agent,"Resumed for PR 119 round-1 blocking retype race. General rule: every successful persistence/read-back path must apply the same complete native envelope contract as its consumers, including type, ownership tag, content identity and provenance. Auditing all immutable creators, readers, SDK/CLI summaries and installed consumers for weaker acceptance predicates; adding real peer retyping/corruption transitions at every new persistence boundary and a function-only revert proof. The branch is current with origin/main (zero behind). Also inspecting the published non-blocking CodeQL shell/path finding and all analogous subprocess sites; unavailable bot reviews are not approval."
  "2026-10-29T11:19:36.511Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: every production native create (including controller authority, environment/run/generation/card, benchmark/evaluation/episode/outcome, sweep/transfer, evaluation plans, shadow receipts, process jobs and meta reservations) now shares SDK birth/current read-back validation of native type, body, ownership tags, provenance and relationships. Influence producer and reader share ownedRecord. Mutable title/status annotations remain accepted; ordinary writers still have a documented window after the final read. No lease-isolation claim or peer-data compensation was added. Revert proof: removing only ownedRecord type validation fails the adversarial ownership test (1 failed); restored function passes (1 passed). Removing only createVerifiedItem envelope comparison likewise fails the package-wide producer contract (1 failed), restored passes (1 passed). Existing slice-effect and durable-version revert proofs still fail/pass as intended. CodeQL alert 3 is factually a false positive: execFileSync already uses argv without shell interpolation, and fixed command-v discovery contains no untrusted text. Explicit shell:false plus literal shell-metacharacter artifact names now assert this behavior in every packed install mode; no suppressions or weakened tests."
  "2026-10-29T11:28:17.594Z",codex-agent,"Current revision targeted checks: strict typecheck and changed-file lint pass; duplicate gate reports zero clones; isolated pm linked-test run passes 2/2 new class regressions, including adversarial changes before every SDK read and immediately after creation. Remaining related evaluation-plan/policy-card/shadow suites and the unchanged 500-sequence influence model are running with concurrency 2. Full npm/Bun release-gate evidence remains assigned to CI under the original saturated-host constraint; package coverage runs use concurrency 1 and release prechecks use 2. No host Docker access is authorized or used. Public CLI version remains 2026.10.28; SDK pin remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T11:35:38.987Z",codex-agent,"Class audit found two further predicate mismatches and they are being closed rather than deferred: policy-card publication/batch preflight allowed a removed ownership tag even though discovery skipped that record; a retained historical snapshot cannot establish the current native envelope for either a card or an influence report. Retained-card publication, preflight and ancestry now share one predicate; latest influence reads and card ancestry re-read current SDK state after historical certification, while explicit historical citations keep their historical semantics. The first fresh packed run exposed an installed CLI show succeeding after a real peer retype; packed acceptance correctly failed and those bytes are not final evidence. Added dedicated producer/discovery/ancestry regressions and retained all existing tests."
  "2026-10-29T11:43:46.779Z",codex-agent,"Installed-host root cause established with real SDK/CLI reads: the pinned SDK emits compact history oldest-first, while CLI 2026.10.28 emits newest-first. The old last-row lookup selected revision 1 after a peer had retyped revision 2. This is a package presentation-order assumption, not an upstream defect claim. Removed the assumption in every compact-history consumer: influence latest reads choose the greatest durable coordinate; policy citations and promotion attribution choose the earliest qualifying durable coordinate through one validated ordering function. A 500-permutation property test uses actual native history rows, rejects invalid/repeated coordinates, verifies fixed read-back, and injects a real retype after historical capture. Explicit historical citations remain usable; current reads revalidate current ownership separately."
  "2026-10-29T11:47:26.635Z",codex-agent,"Focused class validation now passes 5/5 (SDK native-create guard, 500 native-history permutations, card producer/discovery ownership, every influence persistence boundary, compacted durable versions). Separate actual recursive consumers pass 2/2: removed ancestor ownership tags refuse, and reversed native history preserves earliest card citations plus the original promotion author after another author annotates the generation. All production compact-history access now routes through the shared certified coordinate validator; all native creates route through SDK birth/current validation. The wider related suite remains running at concurrency 2; no existing test has been deleted or weakened."
  "2026-10-29T12:12:37.083Z",codex-agent,"Fresh exact artifact passes all five installed-consumer modes: npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx and project-local on CLI 2026.10.28 with Git absent. Each passes six typed JSON/TOON foreign-record refusals (30 total) after a real peer retypes the native report; retry, show and proposal feedback agree, preserve peer state, and create no foreign proposal file. All modes also accept a literal shell-metacharacter artifact filename without interpolation. Compact show remains 1133 JSON bytes and 837 TOON bytes. Artifact SHA-256 6e489d1f0979cbcab08b0476cdcbbfc0a8a1e6a357ed59ae725f4a9426b908e6, 817981 bytes; all 226 shipped files match source. An isolated ignored shipped-file mutation yields exactly one mismatch; restoration yields zero; reviewed source and captured artifact are untouched. Strict isolated tracker health, full lint, test type compilation, typecheck, docstrings (418 declarations/55 sources) and zero-duplicate checks pass. Expanded function-only revert harness is being diagnosed before its new proofs are counted."
  "2026-10-29T12:15:24.336Z",codex-agent,"The broader related local run reached the pre-existing 600-second timeout in the 512-case canonical policy-card property test on the saturated host (timeout, not a failed value assertion). Stopped only that verified test process family after the failure; do not count the broad run as green. No test, assertion, timeout, threshold or worker limit is weakened. Full npm/Bun release gates remain required in CI, and the final head must retain any pending status honestly. Running the feature suite alone now gives current-snapshot evidence for its 500-operation SDK state model without the unrelated heavy fault matrix competing for host resources."
  "2026-10-29T12:25:19.658Z",codex-agent,"Final isolated feature suite passes 12/12, zero fail/skip/cancel, including all 500 seeded native-state operation sequences and 500 history permutations. Expanded disposable function-only revert run now completes successfully without changing assertions or timeouts: 9 mutants each fail exactly one selected regression, and all 9 restorations pass. Functions: measureTrainingInfluence, readTrainingInfluence durable-version addressing, promotionAuthor, policy snapshot, orderedHistoryEntries, readTrainingInfluence current-envelope validation, matchingRetainedCard, ownedRecord and createVerifiedItem. The earlier failed restored run is not counted as passing evidence; the complete fresh run is green. Each mutation touches only its named function in a disposable copy, and the reviewed package source remains unchanged. Existing 512-case broader card-suite timeout remains an honest local limitation pending the full CI gates. origin/main was fetched again and remains zero behind."
  "2026-10-29T12:37:05.538Z",codex-agent,"The package-wide native identity audit reproduced one final instance with the real SDK: project prefix training- creates an already-qualified training-influence ID, but the reader suffix heuristic falsely refused the producer record. General rule: native target identities must use the SDK canonicalizer, never hand-written prefix/suffix normalization. Replacing the lone report identity heuristic with normalizeItemId; other remaining hash-suffix checks bind content digests, and other native namespace ownership checks already use SDK canonical identifiers. Added four real project-prefix round trips with retry/proposal verification, included config reads in interleaving boundaries, and made npm/Bun global packed modes use the colliding prefixes. New function-only revert and fresh captured artifact validation are required before finalizing."
  "2026-10-29T13:09:23.389Z",codex-agent,"Final unchanged-source managed run: pm test pm-rl-measured-influence --run --only-index 1 --progress passes 13/13, zero failures/skips/cancellations, including 500 seeded state sequences, 500 native-history permutations, all report read/write/config boundaries, foreign IDs, SDK prefix collisions, compacted versions and recursive feedback. Other managed groups pass 4/4 and 1/1. node test/training-influence.revert.ts passes 10 independent function-only mutants (each 0 pass/1 fail) and 10 restored runs (each 1 pass/0 fail), including SDK-native identity, ordering, ownership and post-create verification. Final packed artifact d326560e5b7ff1f220eb75ad77fa8dfece2fc4dbab5e00bbf31f663caada71d7 is 818087 bytes; all 226 files match source and an isolated ignored-file mutation is detected. Five installation modes pass 30 foreign JSON/TOON refusals; npm/Bun global cover training- and training-influence- prefixes. Packets are 1130-1133 JSON bytes and 834-837 TOON bytes. Lint, type/test compilation, docstrings and duplicate checks pass. Earlier broader 512-case card property timeout is retained as a local limitation, not approval; the exact-head npm/Bun CI gates remain required. No new upstream pm CLI/SDK defect established; supported history presentation and ID normalization differences are handled in-package. Leave the item open for orchestrator verification; no merge or release performed."
